    "source_semantic_class": "normative_medication_recommendation",
    "title_or_context": "s suggest that enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneously once daily,<sup>1,13</sup> unfractionated heparin 5000 units subcutaneously every 8 or 12 hours,<sup>14-17</sup> or rivaroxaban 10 mg once daily<sup>11</sup> will radiographically reduce demonstrable venous thrombosis. Effects on mortality or clinically significant pulmonary embolism rates are unclear. For obese patients, a higher dose of enoxaparin 60 mg once daily achieved target range of thromboprophylaxis without increased bleeding.<sup>12</sup>"
